<theodulf. carm. 9.1>	Namque imitatur eum pietate vel actibus almis,
<theodulf. carm. 9.2>	Qui nobis et herus et pater almus inest.
<theodulf. carm. 9.3>	Cui pietas inmensa manet, clementia dulcis,
<theodulf. carm. 9.4>	Qui precibus dignis semper adesse solet.
<theodulf. carm. 9.5>	Non tantum hic veniam scelerum, sed praemia donat,
<theodulf. carm. 9.6>	Conversis placidus, parcere semper amans.
<theodulf. carm. 9.7>	Si pater est et herus nobis deus inclytus, eius
<theodulf. carm. 9.8>	Sectanda est pietas, actio corde, fide.
<theodulf. carm. 9.9>	Discet amare patrem proles, et verna timere,
<theodulf. carm. 9.10>	Hunc amor, illum aptet ad potiora timor.
<theodulf. carm. 9.11>	Degener existit si proles, verna superbus,
<theodulf. carm. 9.12>	Dedecus inmensum foedat utrumque satis.
